---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, OWNER_LOCATION, OWNER_NAME } from '../../consts';

const EFFECTIVE_DATE = 'November 21, 2026';
const contactHref = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;

const collected = [
  'Your name, work email and Microsoft account ID, when you sign in.',
  'Your calendar events, when you connect your Microsoft calendar.',
  'Emails and bookings you review and approve in Meridian. Meridian uses your Microsoft account to send them.',
  'Meeting recordings, transcripts, participant names, join and leave activity, and meeting chat, when you invite the Meridian bot.',
  'Summaries, decisions and action items created from your meetings.',
  'Notes, templates and documents you add, and the questions you ask Meridian.',
  'Your billing name, address, email and payment history. Stripe collects your card. I can see its brand and last 4 digits, never the full number.',
  'Security records, such as sign-ins and important account actions.',
];

const uses = [
  'Record and transcribe the meetings you invite Meridian to.',
  'Write summaries and answer your questions.',
  'Prepare the emails and calendar changes you ask for.',
  'Charge you, send receipts and handle refunds.',
  'Keep the service secure, fix problems and keep the records the law requires.',
];

const providers = [
  { name: 'Recall.ai', job: 'joins meetings, records them and creates transcripts.' },
  { name: 'Anthropic', job: 'processes meeting content and questions so its Claude AI can write summaries and answers.' },
  { name: 'Microsoft', job: 'handles sign-in, calendar access and the emails you approve.' },
  { name: 'Railway', job: 'hosts the Meridian app and its database.' },
  { name: 'Stripe', job: 'processes payments, receipts and invoices, and helps prevent fraud.' },
  { name: 'GitHub and Google Fonts', job: 'deliver this web page and may receive your IP address.' },
];
---

<Base title="Meridian privacy policy" description="How Meridian collects, uses and protects personal information, including meeting recordings.">
  <section class="container reading page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
    <h1>Meridian privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
      Meridian is an AI meeting assistant sold by {OWNER_NAME}, based in {OWNER_LOCATION}. I am
      responsible for the personal information described here.
    </p>

    <h2>What Meridian collects</h2>
    <ul>{collected.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>

    <h2>How it is used</h2>
    <ul>{uses.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
    <p>I do not sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2>If you are in a recorded meeting</h2>
    <p>
      The Meridian bot joins under a visible name and posts a notice in meeting chat saying it is
      recording and transcribing. If you do not consent, ask the host to remove it. The person who
      invites Meridian is responsible for having the right to record that meeting. If you were
      recorded and want to ask about your information, email
      <a href={contactHref}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see your information</h2>
    <p>
      Your meetings, notes and documents are tied to your account. If you share an answer, summary or
      email, the people who receive it can read it and may copy it. The people who operate Meridian
      have technical access to its systems and may use it to fix problems or keep the service secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Who I share it with</h2>
    <p>I share only what these providers need to do their job:</p>
    <ul>
      {
        providers.map((provider) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{provider.name}</strong> {provider.job}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you connect another AI assistant, such as ChatGPT, Claude or Codex, it receives the Meridian
      information you allow it to read under that company's own terms. I may also disclose
      information when the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Meeting recordings and transcripts are processed in the United States. Other providers may also
      store or process your information outside Canada, where it may be subject to the laws of that
      country.
    </p>

    <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Meetings, notes and documents stay until you delete them or ask me to. Permanently deleting a
      meeting in Meridian also asks Recall.ai to delete its recording. After you cancel, email me to
      have your account deleted. Billing records are kept for at least 6 years for tax purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Meridian uses essential cookies to keep you signed in and protect sign-in. It does not use
      advertising or analytics cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to see, correct or delete your personal information, or withdraw your consent, by
      emailing <a href={contactHref}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Some records must be kept by law. If you are
      not satisfied with my answer, you can contact the Office of the Information and Privacy
      Commissioner of Alberta.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, I will update the date at the top. Questions go to
      <a href={contactHref}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--cognac-dark);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
